# InterviewIQ AI: v0 Frontend Prompt Pack

Build the frontend in **7 parts**, each in a separate v0 account. For every part, paste **SHARED CONTEXT (Section B) first, then that part's prompt**. Shared Context is what makes the parts fit together when you merge them.

---

## A. How to use this pack

1. Create a Next.js project locally (`npx create-next-app@latest interviewiq --ts --tailwind --app`), then run `npx shadcn@latest init`.
2. For each Part N: open a v0 account, paste **Section B + Part N prompt**, generate, then download or copy the files listed under **"Files to copy"**.
3. **Part 1 owns all shared files** (`lib/*`, `app/layout.tsx`, `app/globals.css`, `middleware.ts`, `components/shared/*`, `components/app-shell/*`, `app/(app)/layout.tsx`). From Parts 2–7 **never copy those files**. Copy only the files listed for that part. If two parts generated the same file, Part 1's version wins.
4. All `components/ui/*` files are standard shadcn, so they are identical everywhere. Copy any that are missing, or run `npx shadcn@latest add button card badge ...`.
5. Install dependencies once: `npm i @clerk/nextjs @clerk/themes recharts lucide-react sonner next-themes date-fns`.

**Merge order:** Part 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5 → 6 → 7.

### Environment variables (`.env.local`; also add to each v0 project's Vars panel for preview)
```
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxx
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/sign-up
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_FALLBACK_REDIRECT_URL=/dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_FALLBACK_REDIRECT_URL=/dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK=true
```
`NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK=true` lets the whole UI run on mock data before the FastAPI backend exists. Set it to `false` when the backend is ready.

### Clerk dashboard setup (2 minutes)
1. Create an application at clerk.com and enable **Email** and **Google** under *User & Authentication → Social connections*.
2. Copy the publishable and secret keys into `.env.local`.
3. In *Paths*, set sign-in to `/sign-in`, sign-up to `/sign-up`, and the after-auth URL to `/dashboard`.
4. If you use Next.js 16, name the middleware file `proxy.ts` instead of `middleware.ts`. The contents are the same.

