=== SHARED CONTEXT: INTERVIEWIQ AI (do not deviate; this project is built in parts by different people and merged) ===

PRODUCT
InterviewIQ AI is a voice-based AI mock interviewer for students and job seekers. The candidate picks an interview type, the AI interviewer SPEAKS a question (Gnani Timbre text-to-speech), the candidate answers by voice, the answer is transcribed (Gnani Prisma speech-to-text), evaluated against a rubric, and an adaptive follow-up question is spoken back. At the end the candidate gets a scored performance report. Build FRONTEND ONLY. A separate FastAPI backend exists; every data call goes through lib/api.ts.

STACK (fixed)
Next.js App Router + TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, lucide-react icons, Recharts, sonner (toasts), next-themes (dark/light), date-fns, Clerk (@clerk/nextjs, @clerk/themes). No other UI libraries. Use "use client" only where needed. Import alias "@/".

DESIGN SYSTEM (use semantic Tailwind tokens like bg-background, text-muted-foreground, bg-primary, border-border; NEVER hardcode hex colors inside components)
- Font: Inter via next/font (var --font-sans). Also load Noto Sans Tamil (--font-tamil) and Noto Sans Devanagari (--font-hindi) so Tamil/Hindi transcript text renders correctly.
- Tokens in app/globals.css (HSL shadcn variables), light + dark. Dark mode is DEFAULT (class strategy via next-themes, defaultTheme="dark").
