## G. PART 5: Interview Room (core voice experience)

**Paste into: Account 5.** This is the most important part.

````
[PASTE SHARED CONTEXT HERE]

PART 5 TASK: Build the live voice interview room. This page is immersive: it must NOT use the sidebar shell.

Files:
- app/(interview)/layout.tsx: minimal layout, full-height bg-background with a subtle radial gradient, no sidebar. Just {children}.
- app/(interview)/session/[sessionId]/page.tsx: "use client" page composing the components below.
- hooks/use-audio-recorder.ts
- hooks/use-audio-player.ts
- components/session/* (listed below)

1. HOOK useAudioRecorder()
   Returns { status: 'idle'|'requesting'|'recording'|'stopped'|'error', error?: string, durationMs, level (0..1 live input level), blob: Blob | null, start(), stop(), reset(), analyser: AnalyserNode | null }.
   - Request the mic with getUserMedia({ audio: { echoCancellation: true, noiseSuppression: true } }).
   - Choose the mimeType using MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported in this order: 'audio/webm;codecs=opus', 'audio/webm', 'audio/mp4'. Collect chunks, build the Blob on stop.
   - Level meter via AudioContext + AnalyserNode (requestAnimationFrame), update level ~30fps.
   - Auto-stop at 120 seconds. Clean up tracks, AudioContext and rAF on stop/unmount. Map errors to friendly messages (NotAllowedError → "Microphone access was blocked", NotFoundError → "No microphone found").
2. HOOK useAudioPlayer()
   Returns { speak(text: string, audioUrl?: string | null, lang: Language): Promise<void>, stop(), isSpeaking, error }.
   - If audioUrl exists, play it with an HTMLAudioElement and resolve when it ends.
   - If audioUrl is null/missing or fails to load, FALL BACK to window.speechSynthesis (voice lang en-IN for 'en', ta-IN for 'ta', hi-IN for 'hi') so the demo works even without the TTS backend. Resolve on end. Handle autoplay restrictions by catching play() rejections and returning a flag so the UI can show a "Tap to play question" button.
3. PAGE LOGIC (state machine)
   phase: 'intro' | 'asking' | 'ready' | 'recording' | 'review' | 'processing' | 'finishing' | 'error'.
   - On mount read sessionStorage[SESSION_STORAGE_KEY(sessionId)] → { config, firstQuestion, startedAt }. If missing, toast and router.replace('/setup').
   - 'intro': a centered card "Ready when you are" with the interview summary (ConfigBadges), a mic permission check (request permission here), tips, and a big "Begin interview" button. The click is the user gesture that unlocks audio playback.
   - 'asking': the interviewer speaks the current question (useAudioPlayer.speak). The VoiceOrb is in 'speaking' state; question text shown as live captions. A "Skip audio" ghost button and "Replay question" button are available. When finished → 'ready'.
   - 'ready': VoiceOrb 'idle'; a prominent circular mic button "Tap to answer" (spacebar also toggles).
   - 'recording': orb 'listening', live waveform (<Waveform /> driven by analyser/level), elapsed timer, "Tap to stop" (a red stop button; Space/Enter also stop). Minimum 1.5 s recording; if shorter, toast "That was too short. Try again." and reset.
   - 'review': after stopping, show an audio preview (HTMLAudioElement from the blob URL) with buttons "Re-record" (secondary) and "Submit answer" (primary).
   - 'processing': orb 'thinking'; a 3-step progress stepper that advances on a timer while the request is in flight: "Transcribing your answer (Prisma)…" → "Evaluating…" → "Preparing the next question…". Call submitAnswer(sessionId, currentQuestion.id, blob, token).
   - On success: append the candidate turn (res.transcript) to the transcript; if res.isComplete or !res.nextQuestion → phase 'finishing'; else set currentQuestion = res.nextQuestion, append an interviewer turn, store per-answer evaluation in a ref (for the optional live feedback toggle), go to 'asking'.
   - 'finishing': full-screen "Wrapping up… generating your report" with a thinking orb; call endSession(sessionId, token), clear the sessionStorage entry, then router.push(`/results/${sessionId}`).
   - 'error': friendly card with Retry (resubmit the same blob) and "End interview" actions. Never lose the recorded blob on network errors.
   - Timer: countdown from config.durationMin shown in the top bar. When it reaches 0, show a toast "Time's up. Finish your current answer" and mark `timeUp`; after the current answer is submitted, go to 'finishing' even if the API returns another question. Turn the timer text warning-colored under 60 s.
   - "End interview" button (top bar) opens an AlertDialog ("End interview early? Your answers so far will still be scored."); confirm → 'finishing'.
   - Warn on tab close during an active interview using a beforeunload handler.
4. COMPONENTS in components/session/
   - session-topbar.tsx: Logo (sm), ConfigBadges, question counter "Question 3" with progress dots, countdown timer, "End interview" button.
   - interviewer-panel.tsx: large VoiceOrb centered, status label under it ("Interviewer is speaking…", "Your turn", "Listening…", "Thinking…"), the current question in large readable text (use the Tamil/Hindi font class when config.language is ta/hi), and a "Follow-up" badge with a sparkle icon when question.isFollowUp is true.
   - waveform.tsx: canvas or div-bar waveform driven by `level` / the analyser, 40 bars, smooth.
   - record-controls.tsx: the mic/stop/re-record/submit control cluster with keyboard hint "Press Space".
   - transcript-panel.tsx: right-hand panel (on mobile, a bottom Sheet opened from a "Transcript" button) with chat bubbles (interviewer left, candidate right), auto-scroll to latest, timestamps, and a "Live feedback" Switch (off by default) that, when on, shows each answer's overall score and one improvement tip under the candidate bubble.
   - processing-stepper.tsx: the 3-step animated stepper.
   - intro-card.tsx: the pre-interview card.
   Layout: desktop = two columns (main stage ~65% with interviewer + controls, transcript ~35%); mobile = single column with the transcript in a Sheet.
5. Accessibility and resilience: aria-live="polite" region announcing phase changes, focus management on the main action button, reduced-motion support, handle `visibilitychange` (pause nothing, but stop the player if the user leaves).

Everything must work in mock mode: with audioUrl null the browser speech synthesis speaks the questions, and the mock submitAnswer returns the next question.
